-- 0174: Jamhara weak-letter bin, second pass — 1,501 blocks take the root of the article they sit in (method
-- 'jamhara_neighbour'): 312 between two blocks of the same root, 1,189 verse lines / quotation intros / continuations
-- that follow their article up to the next headword. Never across a group head. Read 20/20 per tier (agent), 14/14 (main).
-- Also: three «قَوْله:» glosses on a verse that 0172 filed under قول go back to the bin — they are not قول headwords.
-- jam_rekey2: Jamhara weak-letter bin, second pass — a block with no headword of its own takes the root of its
-- neighbours, in the edition's reading order (same root_entry_id, by block_seq). Follows AL 0172 (jamhara_headword).
-- Touches ar_ling_lexicon_block_rekey ONLY. Every statement is guarded by method = 'jamhara_group_head', the old root
-- (خوو / يهيه / راي) and an explicit block_id list; sets method = 'jamhara_neighbour'. Not applied.
--
-- Tier A    312  a still-unresolved block between two resolved blocks (jamhara_headword / manual) of the SAME root,
--                with only unresolved blocks between them and no group head «(…)»/«[…]», chapter header, «٣ -»
--                or «أُهملت» in the gap; every block in the gap must have no headword of its own, or one that fits
--                the root (else the whole gap is skipped: 55 gaps).
-- Tier B   1189  verse lines, «قال الشاعر:» / «وأنشد:» intros, «أي …» continuations and «تعالى» / «عزّ وجلّ»
--                fragments that directly follow a resolved block, up to the next block with a headword, a group
--                head, a chapter header, «٣ -» or «أُهملت». Also required: the resolved block's LAST sub-headword is
--                its own root (so a verse illustrating a later word in that block is not misfiled), no headword in the
--                block's body points elsewhere, and a run of verse lines carries a word of the root.
-- total    1501  blocks → 398 roots; by old key: خوو 1468, راي 6, يهيه 27
--   Tier A by class: ambiguous 21, unresolved 291
--   Tier B by class: continuation (starts mid-discussion) 38, fragment (تعالى / عز وجل) 37, poetry/verse line 1086, quotation intro 28
-- Every target root is a lookup key of itself in ar_ling_root_lexicon_key (checked live), so the blocks stay visible in
-- ar_ling_root_lexicon_block_v.
-- Eye check (jam_rekey2.md): Tier A 20/20 right; Tier B 20/20 right on the final rules (two earlier rounds found
-- 3/20 and 1/20 wrong; the rules were tightened after each and the sample redrawn).
-- Dry run on a local SQLite copy of the 21,090 rekey rows of the two entries: 1501 rows change, a second run
-- changes nothing, jamhara_headword / manual rows untouched.
-- Generated 2026-10-07 from a read of the live AL D1.

